  "body": "**[Original report](https://bitbucket.org/agriggio/art/issues/205) by John Tompkins (Bitbucket: [John Tompkins](https://bitbucket.org/John Tompkins), ).**\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nI recently purchased a 34 inch 3440x1440 ultawide screen monitor. That's a 21:9 aspect ratio. I notice in the crop tool the predefined crop ratios don't include 21:9. I realize the aspect ratio of the monitor doesn't require the same aspect ratio for the image but sometimes its handy. From what I see the only change needed to allow a 21:9 crop would be to add a single line to [rtgui](http://rtgui.cc)/crop.cc in the crop\\_ratios array under the Crop::Crop\\(\\) constructor. Would it be that easy and would it be useful to others? Perhaps there is more I am missing. Thoughts?\n",
